## LAN server

Run `./serve.sh` and open `http://<computer-ip>:8000/` on the reader.

## Android localhost server

The `android/` project packages the current `index.html` into a small APK. On launch it starts a localhost-only HTTP server on port `8080` and opens the reader browser at:

`http://127.0.0.1:8080/`

Build it with Android SDK/Gradle installed:

```sh
cd android
gradle assembleDebug
```

Install the resulting `android/app/build/outputs/apk/debug/app-debug.apk`, then launch `MTG Life Counter`. The service stays alive using a foreground notification where supported.

The same workflows are available through `Makefile`:

```sh
make env
make server
make apk
make install-apk
```

Use `make server PORT=8080` for another LAN port. Use `make apk GRADLE=./gradlew` when the repository has a Gradle wrapper.
